{"id":"n2-164","title":"～わけではない (〜wake dewa nai)","jlptLevel":2,"shortExplanation":"Not necessarily; it doesn't mean that ~.","longExplanation":"The ～わけではない grammar point is used to express that something is not necessarily the case or 'it doesn’t mean that...' It negates a broad assumption or generalization.","formation":"Verb-plain + わけではない, い-Adjective + わけではない, な-Adjective + だわけではない, Noun + だわけではない","examples":[{"jp":"彼が勉強しないわけではないが、成績があまり良くない。","romaji":"Kare ga benkyou shinai wake dewa nai ga, seiseki ga amari yoku nai.","en":"It's not that he doesn't study, but his grades aren't very good.","words":[{"surface":"彼","vocabId":"1483070","reading":"かれ"},{"surface":"が","vocabId":null},{"surface":"勉強","vocabId":"1512670","reading":"べんきょう"},{"surface":"し","vocabId":"1310720","reading":"し","baseForm":"する"},{"surface":"ない","vocabId":null},{"surface":"わけ","vocabId":"1538330","reading":"わけ"},{"surface":"で","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"だ"},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"ない","vocabId":"2098290","reading":"ない"},{"surface":"が","vocabId":null},{"surface":"、","vocabId":null},{"surface":"成績","vocabId":"1375760","reading":"せいせき"},{"surface":"が","vocabId":null},{"surface":"あまり","vocabId":"1584930","reading":"あまり"},{"surface":"良く","vocabId":"1605870","reading":"よく","baseForm":"良い"},{"surface":"ない","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[5,6,7,8]},{"jp":"このレストランが高いわけではないけど、毎日通うには少し高いね。","romaji":"Kono resutoran ga takai wake dewa nai kedo, mainichi kayou ni wa sukoshi takai ne.","en":"It's not that this restaurant is expensive, but it's a bit too pricey to go there every day.","words":[{"surface":"この","vocabId":null},{"surface":"レストラン","vocabId":null},{"surface":"が","vocabId":null},{"surface":"高い","vocabId":"1283190","reading":"たかい"},{"surface":"わけ","vocabId":"1538330","reading":"わけ"},{"surface":"で","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"だ"},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"ない","vocabId":null},{"surface":"けど","vocabId":null},{"surface":"、","vo